{
  "why": [
    "VDS180 — how each bento consumer looks, measured by `pnpm look:census` in a",
    "browser, route by route, in three views: desktop dark, desktop light and a",
    "390 px phone. Every figure is split by who wrote the element: `package` for",
    "this package's components, `product` for the product's own source, `unknown`",
    "where React left no stack to read.",
    "",
    "This is the first reading, and it is the allowance: a later run fails when a",
    "figure's distinct count grows past it, so each task in the look round lowers",
    "a number here with `--write` rather than claiming an improvement. `offenders`",
    "names, per value, the routes carrying anything but the most common value.",
    "`crowded` is the routes painting more than one button in --primary, and",
    "`dock` the routes where the shell's corner or dock covers a control, and",
    "`tiles` (VDS187) the routes drawing a list as a mosaic rather than a table.",
    "",
    "Routes are the router's own patterns, read from the page, so no id or",
    "account name is written here. A consumer this machine could not load stays",
    "listed with the reason, so the gap is a line and not a silence."
  ],
